              <TR>
                <TD class=3Dheader vAlign=3Dtop><SPAN =
class=3Dh1p>SmartDraw UML=20
                  Center</SPAN><BR><SPAN class=3Dh2p>HOW TO DRAW UML =
DIAGRAMS=20
                  (cont'd)</SPAN></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD vAlign=3Dtop><BR><A name=3Dwhatuse></A><SPAN =
class=3Dh2p>What is=20
                  a UML Use Case Diagram?</SPAN></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD>Use case diagrams model the functionality of a =
system=20
                  using actors and use cases. Use cases are services or=20
                  functions provided by the system to its users. =
</TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD><BR><BR></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD vAlign=3Dtop><A name=3Dbasuse></A><SPAN =
class=3Dh2p>Basic Use=20
                  Case Diagram Symbols and Notations</SPAN></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD><BR><BR></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD align=3Dmiddle>
                  <TABLE cellSpacing=3DO cellPadding=3D4 border=3D0>
                    <TBODY>
                    <TR>
                      <TD align=3Dmiddle><IMG height=3D191 alt=3D""=20
                        =
src=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/images/systemuse.g=
if"=20
                        width=3D212 border=3D0> </TD>
                      <TD vAlign=3Dtop><B>System</B><BR>Draw your =
system's=20
                        boundries using a rectangle that contains use =
cases.=20
                        Place actors outside the system's boundries. =
</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD colSpan=3D2><BR><BR></TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD align=3Dmiddle><IMG height=3D64 alt=3D""=20
                        =
src=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/images/usecaseprin=
t.gif"=20
                        width=3D135 border=3D0> </TD>
                      <TD vAlign=3Dtop><B>Use Case</B><BR>Draw use cases =
using=20
                        ovals. Label with ovals with verbs that =
represent the=20
                        system's functions. </TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD colSpan=3D2><BR><BR></TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD align=3Dmiddle><IMG height=3D161 alt=3D""=20
                        =
src=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/images/actors.gif"=
=20
                        width=3D118 border=3D0> </TD>
                      <TD vAlign=3Dtop><B>Actors</B><BR>Actors are the =
users of=20
                        a system. When one system is the actor of =
another=20
                        system, label the actor system with the actor=20
                        stereotype. </TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD colSpan=3D2><BR><BR></TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD align=3Dmiddle><IMG height=3D202 alt=3D""=20
                        =
src=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/images/relationshi=
pusecase.gif"=20
                        width=3D196 border=3D0> </TD>
                      <TD =
vAlign=3Dtop><B>Relationships</B><BR>Illustrate=20
                        relationships between an actor and a use case =
with a=20
                        simple line. For relationships among use cases, =
use=20
                        arrows labeled either "uses" or "extends." A =
"uses"=20
                        relationship indicates that one use case is =
needed by=20
                        another in order to perform a task. An "extends" =

                        relationship indicates alternative options under =
a=20
                        certain use case.<BR><A=20
                        =
href=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/uml8.htm#conn"=20
                        target=3Dnew>Learn how to draw =
relationships</A>.=20
                    </TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD><BR><BR></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD vAlign=3Dtop><A name=3Dwhatseq></A><SPAN =
class=3Dh2p>What is a=20
                  UML Sequence Diagram?</SPAN></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD>Sequence diagrams describe interactions among =
classes in=20
                  terms of an exchange of messages over time. </TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD><BR><BR></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD vAlign=3Dtop><A name=3Dbasseq></A><SPAN =
class=3Dh2p>Basic=20
                  Sequence Diagram Symbols and =
Notations</SPAN></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD><BR><BR></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD align=3Dmiddle>
                  <TABLE cellSpacing=3DO cellPadding=3D4 border=3D0>
                    <TBODY>
                    <TR>
                      <TD align=3Dmiddle><IMG height=3D54 alt=3D""=20
                        =
src=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/images/classrole.g=
if"=20
                        width=3D138 border=3D0><BR><BR></TD>
                      <TD vAlign=3Dtop><B>Class roles</B><BR>Class roles =

                        describe the way an object will behave in =
context. Use=20
                        the UML object symbol to illustrate class roles, =
but=20
                        don't list object attributes.<BR><A=20
                        =
href=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/uml10.htm#addtext=
">Learn=20
                        how to edit text on a symbol</A>.<BR></TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD colSpan=3D2><BR><BR></TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD align=3Dmiddle><IMG height=3D233 alt=3D""=20
                        =
src=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/images/activiation=
.gif"=20
                        width=3D190 border=3D0><BR><BR></TD>
                      <TD =
vAlign=3Dcenter><B>Activation</B><BR>Activation boxes=20
                        represent the time an object needs to complete a =
task.=20
                        <BR><BR></TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD colSpan=3D2><BR><BR></TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD vAlign=3Dtop><IMG height=3D252 alt=3D""=20
                        =
src=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/images/messages.gi=
f"=20
                        width=3D192 border=3D0> </TD>
                      <TD vAlign=3Dtop><B>Messages</B><BR>Messages are =
arrows=20
                        that represent communication between objects. =
Use=20
                        half-arrowed lines to represent asynchronous =
messages.=20
                        Asynchronous messages are sent from an object =
that will=20
                        not wait for a response from the receiver before =

                        continuing its tasks. <BR><A=20
                        =
href=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/uml8.htm#conn">Le=
arn=20
                        how to draw messages</A>.<BR><BR><IMG =
height=3D237 alt=3D""=20
                        =
src=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/images/messagetype=
.gif"=20
                        width=3D240 border=3D0><BR><BR><I>Various =
message types for=20
                        Sequence and Collaboration diagrams</I> =
</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD colSpan=3D2><BR><BR></TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD align=3Dmiddle><IMG height=3D252 alt=3D""=20
                        =
src=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/images/lifelines.g=
if"=20
                        width=3D191 border=3D0> </TD>
                      <TD vAlign=3Dcenter><B>Lifelines</B><BR>Lifelines =
are=20
                        vertical dashed lines that indicate the object's =

                        presence over time.<BR><A=20
                        =
href=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/uml8.htm#dropshap=
">Learn=20
                        how to attach activation boxes to lifelines</A>. =
</TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD colSpan=3D2><BR><BR></TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD align=3Dmiddle><IMG height=3D220 alt=3D""=20
                        =
src=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/images/destroy.gif=
"=20
                        width=3D144 border=3D0> </TD>
                      <TD vAlign=3Dcenter><B>Destroying =
Objects</B><BR>Objects=20
                        can be terminated early using an arrow labeled=20
                        =
"&lt;&nbsp;&lt;&nbsp;destroy&nbsp;&gt;&nbsp;&gt;" that=20
                        points to an X.<BR></TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD colSpan=3D2><BR><BR></TD></TR>
                    <TR>
                      <TD align=3Dmiddle><IMG height=3D239 alt=3D""=20
                        =
src=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/images/loop.gif"=20
                        width=3D192 border=3D0> </TD>
                      <TD vAlign=3Dcenter><B>Loops</B><BR>A repetition =
or loop=20
                        within a sequence diagram is depicted as a =
rectangle.=20
                        Place the condition for exiting the loop at the =
bottom=20
                        left corner in square brackets =
[&nbsp;&nbsp;].<BR><A=20
                        =
href=3D"http://www.smartdraw.com/tutorials/software-uml/uml11.htm#sendbac=
k">Learn=20
                        how to arrange objects on a page</A>.=20
                  </TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></TD></TR>
              <TR>
                <TD><BR><BR></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></TD></TR>
